<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.WebAssembly">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RuntimeIdentifier>browser-wasm</RuntimeIdentifier>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>

    <!-- Required: the JSImport/JSExport source generator emits pointer code. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>

    <!--
      Globalization is left ON, but the reasoning has been measured and narrowed.
      See dotnet/Toolbox.Wasm.Tests/GlobalizationDependencyTests.cs, which runs the
      suite both ways (DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=1) to keep this honest.

      What the measurement found:
        - The old note asked for proof that IgnoreCase still behaves for non-ASCII
          without ICU. It does. Simple Unicode case mapping has lived in CoreLib
          since .NET 5, so accented Latin, Cyrillic and Greek all still match. 242
          of 244 tests pass with ICU off, and the two that do not are the probes
          written to detect exactly this.
        - What ICU actually buys is narrower than "the CultureInvariant toggle":
          without it a named culture cannot be constructed at all - GetCultureInfo
          ("tr-TR") throws. In the browser CurrentCulture follows the visitor's
          locale, so ICU is what makes IgnoreCase correct for a Turkish visitor and
          what leaves the toggle with something to switch off. Drop ICU and the
          toggle silently becomes a no-op, which is a UI honesty problem rather
          than a correctness one.
        - The cost is also smaller than the old "~1.5MB": globalizationMode is
          "sharded", so a visitor downloads exactly one shard. EFIGS is 141KB
          brotli / 551KB raw. The ~1.5MB figure counted all three shards
          uncompressed, which no visitor ever pays.

      So the live trade is 141KB against culture-correct matching for non-English
      locales. If that stops being worth it, set this to true AND remove the
      CultureInvariant toggle from the Regex Tester UI rather than shipping a
      switch that does nothing.
    -->
    <InvariantGlobalization>false</InvariantGlobalization>
    <InvariantTimezone>true</InvariantTimezone>

    <PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>
    <WasmEnableWebcil>true</WasmEnableWebcil>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Toolbox.Wasm.Core\Toolbox.Wasm.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
